---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<Layout title="About" description="Who runs Leaving The Matrix and why.">
  <section class="container-prose py-24">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-display-lg uppercase tracking-tight">
      Why this exists.
    </h1>

    <div class="prose-ltm mt-12">
      <p class="lead text-xl text-bone-dim">
        Leaving The Matrix is run by Luke Vasilion — senior frontend engineer by day, full-time
        markets person by night. The community started as a small group of friends asking the same
        questions about positioning, risk, and what to actually do when the tape gets weird.
      </p>

      <h2>The thesis</h2>
      <p>
        Most "stock picking" services fall into two camps: hype machines that disappear when the
        trade goes wrong, or expensive black-box subscriptions that teach you nothing. We're trying
        to be neither. Every call comes with a thesis. Every thesis comes with the parts that could
        kill it. Every closed position gets reviewed honestly, including the losers.
      </p>

      <h2>The framework</h2>
      <p>
        We trade and invest using a layered framework: <strong>quality × discount × smart-money
        confirmation</strong>. Fundamentals first. Valuation second. Insider, congress, and 13F flow
        as the third leg. Technicals as context, not gospel. It's the same framework Nova — our
        in-house trading copilot — uses to score every name we cover.
      </p>

      <h2>The reality</h2>
      <p>
        Trading is hard. Most people lose money. We're not selling a path to retirement; we're
        selling a way to think about markets that, if you put in the work, gives you a real shot.
        Read the disclaimer. Manage your risk. Show up.
      </p>

      <hr />

      <p class="text-bone-mute">
        <em>This page is a placeholder. Luke's full story, photos, and the LTM origin lore drop here once he sends them over.</em>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-16">
      <a href={SITE.discord.subscribe} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-primary">
        Join the Discord
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
